<title>INDIA: India's Kotak Mahindra 96/97 net lower.</title>
<headline>India's Kotak Mahindra 96/97 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		301.55    vs     453.69</p>
<p>    Net sales	     3,612.44    vs   3,026.73</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   1.8     vs	 1.8</p>
<p>    Expenditure	     595.65    vs	359.60</p>
<p>    Interest		1,972.43    vs    1,690.34</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    705.30    vs	523.09</p>
<p>    Tax			  37.5     vs	  nil</p>
<p>Note: Kotak Mahindra Capital is one of India's largest finance companies. The firm said it provided 251.0 million rupees against full provisioning requirements for non-performing assets as per the Reserve Bank of India rules.</p>
<p>Kotak said profitable churning of investment and asset portfolios contributed to a better operating performance in fiscal 1996/97.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
